 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 666501,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What is the final value of i?\n<pre class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i = 1\ncount = 0\nwhile True:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;if i%2 == 0 or i%3 == 0:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;count += 1\n&nbsp;&nbsp;if count &gt;= 5:\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;print(i)\n&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;break\n&nbsp;&nbsp;i += 1\n</pre>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1328556,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">5</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "If <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i = 5</code>, then the condition <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(i%2 == 0 or i%3 == 0)</code> can only be True for <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i =</code> 2, 3, and 4. Hence, the <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">count</code> variable's value will be 4 and as a result the condition for the second if statement <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(count &gt;= 5)</code> will not be True for the loop to terminate, resulting in a non-terminating or infinite loop."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328557,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">8</code>",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "The loop finds the first five numbers that are divisible by <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">2</code> or <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">3</code>. These numbers are <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">2</code>, <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">3</code>, <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">4</code>, <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">6</code>, and <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">8</code>, and thus <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">8</code> is the final <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i</code>'s value."
    },
    {
     "id": 1328558,
     "content_html": "<code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">30</code>",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The condition for increasing the count is <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">(i%2 == 0 or i%3 == 0)</code>. The condition evaluates True for <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">i</code> values 2, 3, 4, 6, and 8, before the loop's termination. "
    }
   ],
